WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.339
Soon Dorothy and her friends received a message from the Wizard of Oz.

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.421
It said, I will see you tomorrow. Do not call the Winged Monkeys.

3
00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:16.312
They all went to sleep and dreamed of the gifts that Oz had promised to give them.

4
00:00:16.313 --> 00:00:20.736
The next morning a soldier came to get them.

5
00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:25.588
He brought them into the Wizard's throne room, and they were shocked to find it empty.

6
00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:32.409
Dorothy and her friends were each expecting to see Oz as he had first appeared to them.

7
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:40.809
"I am Oz, the Great and Terrible. Why do you seek me?" said a deep voice.

8
00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:45.273
Dorothy and her friends looked for the speaker, but they couldn't see anyone.

9
00:00:45.274 --> 00:00:49.314
"Wh—where are you?" asked a frightened Dorothy.

10
00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:54.231
"I am everywhere," answered the voice.

11
00:00:54.232 --> 00:00:58.962
"We have come to claim what was promised to us," continued Dorothy.

12
00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:02.232
"What was promised?" asked Oz.

13
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:06.837
"You promised to help me get back to Kansas," said Dorothy.

14
00:01:06.838 --> 00:01:10.811
"And you promised me a brain," said the Scarecrow.

15
00:01:10.812 --> 00:01:14.065
"You promised me a heart," said the Tin Man.

16
00:01:14.066 --> 00:01:18.585
"And you promised me courage," said the Lion.

17
00:01:18.586 --> 00:01:22.483
"Is the Witch dead?" asked the voice.

18
00:01:22.484 --> 00:01:27.155
"Yes," said Dorothy. "I melted her with water."

19
00:01:27.156 --> 00:01:30.050
"Oh dear," said the voice.

20
00:01:30.051 --> 00:01:34.380
"Well, come to me tomorrow. I need some time to think."

21
00:01:34.381 --> 00:01:39.320
"Time? You've had plenty of time to think!" said the Tin Man angrily.

22
00:01:39.321 --> 00:01:42.713
"We won't wait," agreed the Scarecrow.

23
00:01:42.714 --> 00:01:47.406
"Yes, you must keep your promises," said Dorothy firmly.

24
00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:56.217
The Lion roared quite suddenly because he thought that this might be a good time to frighten the Wizard.

25
00:01:56.218 --> 00:02:04.912
Toto was so startled by the roar that he jumped out of Dorothy's arms and darted behind a curtain.

26
00:02:04.913 --> 00:02:10.867
The curtain fell open, revealing an old man with a bald head and a wrinkled face.

27
00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:14.813
"Who are you?" asked the Tin Man with his ax raised.

28
00:02:14.814 --> 00:02:21.601
"I . . . I am Oz," said the man, trembling. "Don't strike me."

29
00:02:21.602 --> 00:02:25.295
"You are not the Wizard I saw," said Dorothy.

30
00:02:25.296 --> 00:02:30.381
"I . . . I was just pretending," he said.

31
00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:34.303
Oz showed Dorothy and the others how he had fooled them.

32
00:02:34.304 --> 00:02:41.232
Oz had used ropes to make images appear and disappear and mirrors to make things appear bigger and smaller.

33
00:02:41.233 --> 00:02:46.170
Speakers made his voice sound as if it was coming from all around the room.

34
00:02:46.171 --> 00:02:50.128
Oz also told them how he had come to the Emerald City.

35
00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:54.438
"Many years ago I was a balloonist," he said.

36
00:02:54.439 --> 00:02:59.564
"For two days and two nights I could not land my balloon.

37
00:02:59.565 --> 00:03:06.107
On the morning of the third day, the balloon floated over a strange and beautiful country.

38
00:03:06.108 --> 00:03:11.682
The people below saw me come out of the clouds, and they thought I was a wizard.

39
00:03:11.683 --> 00:03:19.656
So when I landed, I just let them go on thinking that's what I was—a wizard."

40
00:03:19.657 --> 00:03:23.996
"I think you are a very bad man!" Dorothy scolded him.

41
00:03:23.997 --> 00:03:30.081
"I am not a bad man, just a bad wizard," said Oz sadly.

42
00:03:30.082 --> 00:03:37.825
"It's true I tricked the people into believing I was a wizard, but I have ruled them well."

43
00:03:37.826 --> 00:03:41.013
"What about my brain?" asked the Scarecrow.

44
00:03:41.014 --> 00:03:45.533
"I can't give you something you already have," said Oz.

45
00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:48.853
"Experience will bring you knowledge."

46
00:03:48.854 --> 00:03:55.436
"That may be true, but I still want you to keep your promise," said the Scarecrow.

47
00:03:55.437 --> 00:03:59.846
"Yes, I want my courage," demanded the Lion.

48
00:03:59.847 --> 00:04:03.216
"You have it already," answered Oz.

49
00:04:03.217 --> 00:04:07.969
"But I still feel scared," replied the Lion.

50
00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.427
"And I want my heart," interrupted the Tin Man.

51
00:04:11.428 --> 00:04:16.156
"A heart will only make you unhappy," said Oz.

52
00:04:16.157 --> 00:04:20.133
"I want to go home," said Dorothy.

53
00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:27.038
Oz looked at each of them and said, "I have pretended to be a wizard for this long.

54
00:04:27.039 --> 00:04:31.400
I guess I can pretend to be a wizard for a little bit longer.

55
00:04:31.401 --> 00:04:35.306
Come back tomorrow. I will give the Scarecrow a brain;

56
00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:40.846
I will give the Lion courage; and I will give the Tin Man a heart."

57
00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:44.819
"What about Dorothy?" asked Dorothy's friends.

58
00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.800
"I shall have to think about that," answered Oz.

59
00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:52.816
"I must think of a way to travel over the Great Desert.

60
00:04:52.817 --> 00:04:58.144
I will think of something, but each of you must promise to keep my secret."

61
00:04:58.145 --> 00:05:02.915
They all agreed.

